From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tyler Baker <tyler.baker@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 18:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] qcom: eliza: use push/pull endpoints in the EVK topology

The Eliza CQS EVK topology ends every PCM stream on the read and write
shared memory endpoint modules. q6apm-dai holds capture periods on a
read endpoint graph to 40 ms or more, so low latency capture is not
possible on the EVK.

Rebuild eliza-cqs-evk-tplg.bin from audioreach-topology d6bb205aca5f
with 95a4d31887d9 ("audioreach: add support for push pull modules")
cherry-picked from Srinivas Kandagatla's push/pull branch, which puts
the push and pull mode shared memory modules at the stream ends.
Built with cmake and alsatplg 1.2.9; the same tree without the
cherry-pick rebuilds the current file byte for byte.

Signed-off-by: Tyler Baker <tyler.baker@oss.qualcomm.com>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [built from audioreach-topology push/pull support that is not merged]
---
